<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6360" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναγνωρ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>recognize,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				258a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Prm.</u>
				127a
			</span></i>, al.:—
				Med.
			,<i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				3.5.5
			</span></i>: 
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				45.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in a tragedy,
				<i>recognize</i> or <i>come to the knowledge</i> of a person
			or thing, so as to produce a <i>dénouement,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1452a36
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>reveal oneself, make oneself known,</i> ib. <i><span class="en">
				1452b5
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>c.</b> causal,
				<i>cause to recognize, reveal oneself to,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				4.59
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>recognize</i> a rule in a new instance, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APr.</u>
				67a24
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
